# Selfhost compiler core rewrite (gc-host overlay)

When work touches wasm32-gc overlay latency, `s2`/`s3` fixpoint on gc+p2,
issue #850, issue #851, fat `MirInst`, whole-module propagate, or
`BOOTSTRAP_EMIT_*`:

- Treat `docs/plans/selfhost-compiler-core-rewrite.md` as the canonical
  executable plan. Decisions are ADR-053.
- This is a **core rewrite**, not an optimization project. Do not start
  `#850` tick 191+ micro hops.
- Search order: remove reasons whole-module fat MIR must stay alive.
  Do not shave one 239s hotspot at a time.
- Acceptance: cacheless flattened `src/compiler/main.ark`, wasm32-gc +
  wasi-p2, `s2 == s3`, 10-run median ≤7s / p95 ≤10s, peak RSS ≤512MB.
  `hello` 2312B / current sha256 is **not** required.
- Do not flip `BOOTSTRAP_EMIT_*` until that acceptance holds.
- Same-condition A/B needs ≥3 runs and ≥10% or revert. Two consecutive
  local-opt misses on one hotspot forbid more local opts there.
- Phase arena (`#850`) is Phase 5. Do not put it first.
- Do not keep a fat `MirInst` reconstruct API. Do not rebuild a `Vec`
  on every generated `_at`.
